    "check": "twelve elected and seven defeated; all nineteen printed votes accounted for.",
    "url": "https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0001480/19550521/117/0007"
  },
  "note": "Election of the Coleraine Borough Council, polled Wednesday 18 May 1955; nineteen candidates for twelve seats (Londonderry Sentinel, 21 May 1955, p. 7). The report states that all twelve successful candidates were Unionists, and that all seven 'workers' nominees were defeated, four of them outgoing members. The newspaper does not print a party label beside each name; the U. label on the twelve follows its summary sentence. The first four places were taken by newcomers."
